# M-held-bytes, panel 124 R6 and panel 125. A lease nobody ends is a leak the
# PROGRAM owes, not the compiler, and the exit-time gate says so in those
# words: `hero_live_blocks` counts what the language owns and would have called
# this "a compiler bug"; the lease has its own counter so the accusation lands
# on the right party. The panic is the whole point of this case, and it is the
# only instrument for it on Darwin arm64, where ASan has no leak detector.

extern "string.h"
    function strlen(s: cstr) -> u64

function main()
    c: cstr @ "twelve bytes".lease()
    print(strlen(s: c))
